{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content -Raw pipeline/goal.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"metric\": {\n    \"name\": \"mIoU\",\n    \"target\": 0.515,\n    \"dataset\": \"ScanRefer\"\n  },\n  \"baseline_experiment_id\": \"AdaRES-B1\",\n  \"description\": \"AdaRES: improve a faithful standard-indicator 3D referring expression segmentation baseline by learning query confidence from metric-aligned evidence, targeting ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.515.\",\n  \"constraints\": [\n    \"Use server-2 GPUs 0 and 1 only; never use server-6.\",\n    \"All experiments launched after AdaRES-B3 must use exactly one GPU; run at most one independent experiment on GPU 0 and one on GPU 1.\",\n    \"Do not design or queue a successor while AdaRES-B3 is running; after B3 reaches a terminal state, admit at most two structurally independent single-GPU candidates.\",\n    \"Use a fixed 30-epoch protocol for the B2 and B4 extension. Resume both from their epoch-20 last checkpoints without resetting the optimizer or LR scheduler; do not tune the epoch count on validation.\",\n    \"Train from the released SPFormer sparse-UNet backbone; the decoder is authored in this project.\",\n    \"Report mIoU, Acc@0.25, Acc@0.5, active queries, latency, and peak memory.\",\n    \"Do not tune thresholds, temperatures, loss weights, feature subsets, or the fixed 30-epoch protocol on ScanRefer validation.\"\n  ],\n  \"banned\": [\n    \"Do not use server-6.\",\n    \"Do not report the released b005/CFNet checkpoints as AdaRES-B0 results.\",\n    \"Do not scan the ranking margin or the occupancy loss weight on validation.\"\n  ],\n  \"pipeline_policy\": {\n    \"research_on_capacity_gap\": true,\n    \"steady_ticks_before_design\": 1,\n    \"fill_to_capacity\": true,\n    \"design_buffer\": 0,\n    \"max_candidates_per_design_tick\": 2\n  }\n}\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content -Raw pipeline/codex_memory.md'","aggregated_output":"# AdaRES_project Research Memory\n\n## Goal And Phase\n- Phase 1 ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.515 unmet; Phase 2 pending. server-2 GPUs 0/1 only, one task per GPU; server-6 excluded.\n- Released SPFormer sparse-UNet backbone and project decoder. No validation tuning of thresholds, temperatures, weights, features, margins or fixed 30-epoch protocol.\n- `research_on_capacity_gap=true`; six hard gates remain diagnosis, controls, native backward, resources, independence and constraints.\n\n## Champion And Baseline\n- B1 0.5020 mIoU, Acc@0.25 0.610, Acc@0.5 0.553, spmIoU 0.467.\n- B4-E30 champion 0.5094, Acc@0.25 0.608, Acc@0.5 0.562, spmIoU 0.474 at epoch 27; target gap 0.0056. B4-E30 continued epoch-20 optimizer/scheduler, not a fresh matched control.\n- B4-E30 best checkpoint: `/bak_home/songcl/Project/AdaRES_project/AdaRES_checkpoints/adares_b4_query_competition_res/20260921_210214/best.pth`.\n\n## Active Hypotheses\n- G1 changes seed/object indicator labels to detached per-query predicted-mask IoU against training targets. Fixed 16-scene B4 diagnosis: 37/240 material errors selected a positive lower-IoU query over a seed-negative oracle. Native backward/resource gates passed; full training outcome pending.\n- No other candidate passes admission. Fixed-subset oracle-mask quality greatly exceeds selected-mask quality, but that is not sufficient to infer a successful confidence mechanism.\n\n## Closed Or Failed Directions\n- B0 0.333; B2-E30 0.5058; B3 0.5014; B4 20-epoch 0.5070; B5 0.5030; C1-E30 0.5008; C2-E30 0.5014; F4 0.5060; D1 0.5080. No tuning-only, seed-repeat or extension-only successor.\n- H5 late global query attention ended 2026-09-26 13:47 +08:00 at best 0.5061 after 30 validations and protected early stop; below B4-E30 by 0.0033. The process had not completed all final training steps. Auxiliary terminal metrics unavailable after monitor log-pull failure.\n- E1 stability, F1 entropy, F2 compactness, F3 seed proximity rejected. H1 sampler omission (0/240), H2 balanced shortlist reduced coverage, H3 score-only 0.38265 versus indicator 0.49186 subset mIoU, H4 relation cohort not enriched; all rejected.\n- J1 pooled mask-language contrast: oracle higher in 123/240 material errors, standalone subset mIoU 0.01315; J2 overlap crowding: oracle higher in 78/240, selected mean crowding 7.936 versus oracle 6.487. Both rejected after fixed 16-scene native screens.\n- K1 sampler-rank shortcut: oracle later in 141/240, higher sampler score in 99/240; sampler-only mIoU 0.34587. K2 mask-area shortcut: oracle larger in 118/240; largest-mask mIoU 0.27271. B4 fixed subset mIoU 0.49186. Both rejected after native 16-scene screens.\n\n## Running And Queue\n- Snapshot 2026-09-26 14:47 +08:00: G1 running server-2 GPU0 best 0.4983 at 29/30, 5/10 nonimproving; GPU1 vacant, no waiting or claiming, active 1/2, candidate budget one. Targeted GPU check: GPU0 22702 MiB, 88%; GPU1 1 MiB, 0%.\n- G1 commit `0f5f695d478b87750d69561428f6421833e629a9`, admission receipt and launch-progress verification recorded. No new candidate enqueued this tick.\n- `research_work.json` latest design cycle attempted K1 and K2, admitted zero, with SHA256 evidence and concrete stop/resume conditions. No due pending candidate.\n\n## Open Questions And Risks\n- No pending questions in prepared manifest. G1 terminal outcome, active queries, full-run latency/peak memory, subgroup effects and evaluation noise remain unknown.\n- H5 30/30 validations did not mean 30 complete training epochs; monitor killed mid-final epoch after patience threshold. Remote log pull failed, so H5 secondary metrics were not inferred.\n- Local Python lacks PyTorch; K1/K2 diagnostic ran in native server-2 environment GPU1. The diagnostic script was copied for read-only research only; no candidate code sync or dispatch.\n- The fixed 16-scene screens are observational, not population or causal efficacy estimates. Negative routes do not establish global hypothesis exhaustion. Resume new independent route with diagnosis and controls, or when G1 terminates.\n\n## Last Tick\n- 2026-09-26 15:04 +08:00 design: monitor and goal preflight succeeded before Codex and were not rerun. K1/K2 native screens rejected, no admission. Analysis, motivation review, design and route decision recorded. GPU1 remains available, subject to all six gates.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content -Raw pipeline/decisions/20260926-150458_route_change.md'","aggregated_output":"# AdaRES_project 决策记录\n\n- **时间**: 2026-09-26 15:04:58\n- **类型**: route_change\n- **问题**: Can sampler rank or mask area explain B4 selection errors enough to fill GPU1?\n- **决策**: Reject K1 and K2 after native fixed-subset screens; leave server-2 GPU1 vacant, G1 on GPU0.\n- **依据**: K1 later oracle 141/240, sampler-only 0.34587; K2 larger oracle 118/240, largest-mask 0.27271; both below B4 subset 0.49186 and fail diagnosis gate.\n- **证据**: pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-K1-K2_negative_diagnosis_20260926-150100.md; pipeline/research_work.json\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content -Raw pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-K1-K2_negative_diagnosis_20260926-150100.md'","aggregated_output":"# Fixed native screens: sampler rank and mask area\n\n2026-09-26 15:01 Asia/Shanghai. B4-E30 best checkpoint, first 16 ScanRefer validation scenes, 441 expressions, 240 material selection errors (oracle minus selected IoU > 0.05). Read-only native server-2 GPU1 inference. Raw paired rows: `AdaRES-K1-K2_native_16scenes_20260926.json`; script: `AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_k1_sampler_rank.py`. These subset observations do not estimate full-validation effects.\n\n| Route | Predeclared mechanism | Paired evidence and controls | Decision |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| K1 sampler-rank shortcut | B4 confidence overuses the sampler's relevance ordering, systematically suppressing later high-IoU queries. | Oracle later than selected in 141/240 errors; oracle sampler score higher in 99/240. Sampler-only top-1 mIoU 0.34587, reversed-order control 0.03610, B4 indicator 0.49186. Sampler-only fixes 50 errors and worsens 43. | Reject this shortcut mechanism. The index difference alone is not causal evidence; no rank-weight scan or training admission. |\n| K2 mask-area shortcut | B4 confidence favors a systematically wrong mask scale over good target masks. | Oracle area larger in 118/240 errors, close to a split. Largest-mask top-1 mIoU 0.27271, smallest-mask 0.00000, versus B4 0.49186; largest-mask fixes 49 errors and worsens 48. | Reject this scale-bias mechanism. No area threshold or fusion scan. |\n\nThe sampler uses descending top-k relevance order, so raw index has a structural interpretation, but the selected-vs-oracle index asymmetry alone does not demonstrate that the head uses rank. K2 uses point-mask area without target information for the controls. Neither passes the diagnosis hard gate; no candidate-specific native backward, resource or admission receipt is claimed. G1 training remains a separate test.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
