{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content -Raw pipeline/reviews/motivation_review_20260926-150100.md'","aggregated_output":"# Motivation Review - AdaRES_project\n\n2026-09-26 15:01 Asia/Shanghai\n\n## 1. Goal\nAdaRES seeks to improve a faithful standard-indicator 3D referring expression segmentation baseline by learning query confidence from metric-aligned evidence, targeting ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.515. B1 0.5020, B4-E30 champion 0.5094, gap 0.0056. Seven goal constraints and three bans remain in force.\n\n## 2. Story Status\n| Hypothesis | Status | Evidence | Gap |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Competition-aware confidence | Partial gain | B4-E30 0.5094 | Target not reached; continuation control is not a fresh matched run |\n| Metric-aligned indicator targets | Training | G1 29/30, best 0.4983 at preflight | Terminal metric and error profile pending |\n| Rank or area shortcut | Disconfirmed as stated | K1/K2 fixed paired native screens | No justified intervention |\n\n## 3. Experiment Assessment\nB1 is 0.5020, B2-E30 0.5058, B4-E30 0.5094, D1 0.5080, F4 0.5060, H5 0.5061; prior closed routes B3, B5, C1/C2 did not reach champion. J1/J2 and K1/K2 do not pass diagnosis. G1 is still running and is not judged by an interim best.\n\n## 4. Gap Analysis\nThe fixed 16-scene oracle 0.87316 versus selected 0.49186 leaves confidence-ordering headroom, but simple rank, mask-area, overlap, pooled-language and earlier structural changes do not provide a validated mechanism for recovering it. Full-run efficiency metrics and matched-control noise are incomplete.\n\n## 5. Design Rationale\nK1 checked whether sampler ordering creates a head shortcut; K2 checked whether mask scale dominates quality mistakes. Their paired counts are weak or contradictory, while standalone controls are worse. Neither advances to a model variant; no validation feature or weight search is justified. A new route requires independent evidence, matched control, backward and resource gates.\n\n## 6. Next Batch\nNo admission (budget one). Keep GPU1 vacant; resume on G1 terminal outcome or new specific evidence for a structurally independent confidence mechanism. See `pipeline/designs/exp_design_20260926-150100.md`.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content -Raw AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_k1_sampler_rank.py'","aggregated_output":"import argparse\nimport json\nimport statistics\nimport sys\nimport types\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport gorilla\nimport torch\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\n\nfrom ipdn.dataset import build_dataset\nfrom ipdn.model_paper5.adares_b4_query_competition import IPDN\nfrom ipdn.utils import get_root_logger\n\n\ndef predictor():\n    def predict_by_feat(\n        self, scan_ids, object_idss, ann_ids, out, superpoints,\n        gt_pmasks, gt_spmasks, fps_seed_sp,\n    ):\n        rows = []\n        for index, target in enumerate(gt_pmasks):\n            superpoint_masks = out[\"masks\"][index].sigmoid().gt(0.5)\n            masks = superpoint_masks[:, superpoints]\n            truth = target.gt(0.5).to(masks.device)\n            ious = (masks & truth).sum(-1).float() / (\n                (masks | truth).sum(-1).clamp_min(1).float()\n            )\n            confidence = F.softmax(out[\"indis\"][index], dim=-1)[:, 1]\n            sampler = out[\"ref_scores\"][index][out[\"sample_inds\"][index]]\n            selected = int(confidence.argmax())\n            oracle = int(ious.argmax())\n            rows.append({\n                \"scene_index\": self.probe_scene_index,\n                \"selected_iou\": float(ious[selected]),\n                \"oracle_iou\": float(ious[oracle]),\n                \"sampler_only_iou\": float(ious[sampler.argmax()]),\n                \"reverse_rank_iou\": float(ious[sampler.argmin()]),\n                \"largest_mask_iou\": float(ious[masks.sum(-1).argmax()]),\n                \"smallest_mask_iou\": float(ious[masks.sum(-1).argmin()]),\n                \"selected_area\": int(masks[selected].sum()),\n                \"oracle_area\": int(masks[oracle].sum()),\n                \"target_area\": int(truth.sum()),\n                \"selected_rank\": selected + 1,\n                \"oracle_rank\": oracle + 1,\n                \"selected_sampler_score\": float(sampler[selected]),\n                \"oracle_sampler_score\": float(sampler[oracle]),\n                \"selected_confidence\": float(confidence[selected]),\n                \"oracle_confidence\": float(confidence[oracle]),\n            })\n        return {\"rows\": rows}\n\n    return predict_by_feat\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    parser.add_argument(\"config\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"checkpoint\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--output\", required=True)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--scenes\", type=int, default=16)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--gpu-id\", type=int, default=1)\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    gorilla.set_cuda_visible_devices([args.gpu_id], 1)\n    gorilla.set_random_seed(1999)\n    cfg = gorilla.Config.fromfile(args.config)\n    data_cfg = cfg.data.val.copy()\n    data_cfg.training = False\n    data_cfg.aug = False\n    data_cfg.with_elastic = False\n    data_cfg.lang_num_max = 32\n    dataset = build_dataset(data_cfg, get_root_logger())\n    model = IPDN(**cfg.model).cuda()\n    checkpoint = torch.load(args.checkpoint, map_location=\"cpu\")\n    loaded = model.load_state_dict(checkpoint.get(\"model\", checkpoint), strict=False)\n    allowed = {\n        \"text_encoder.embeddings.position_ids\",\n        \"text_encoder.embeddings.token_type_ids\",\n    }\n    if loaded.missing_keys or set(loaded.unexpected_keys) - allowed:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Checkpoint mismatch: {loaded}\")\n    model.eval()\n    model.predict_by_feat = types.MethodType(predictor(), model)\n    rows = []\n    for index in range(min(args.scenes, len(dataset))):\n        model.probe_scene_index = index\n        with torch.no_grad():\n            rows.extend(model(dataset.collate_fn([dataset[index]]), mode=\"predict\")[\"rows\"])\n    errors = [r for r in rows if r[\"oracle_iou\"] - r[\"selected_iou\"] > 0.05]\n    result = {\n        \"checkpoint\": args.checkpoint,\n        \"scenes\": min(args.scenes, len(dataset)),\n        \"expressions\": len(rows),\n        \"material_errors\": len(errors),\n        \"indicator_miou\": statistics.fmean(r[\"selected_iou\"] for r in rows),\n        \"sampler_only_miou\": statistics.fmean(r[\"sampler_only_iou\"] for r in rows),\n        \"reverse_rank_miou\": statistics.fmean(r[\"reverse_rank_iou\"] for r in rows),\n        \"largest_mask_miou\": statistics.fmean(r[\"largest_mask_iou\"] for r in rows),\n        \"smallest_mask_miou\": statistics.fmean(r[\"smallest_mask_iou\"] for r in rows),\n        \"error_oracle_later\": sum(\n            r[\"oracle_rank\"] > r[\"selected_rank\"] for r in errors\n        ),\n        \"error_oracle_sampler_higher\": sum(\n            r[\"oracle_sampler_score\"] > r[\"selected_sampler_score\"]\n            for r in errors\n        ),\n        \"error_sampler_better\": sum(\n            r[\"sampler_only_iou\"] > r[\"selected_iou\"] for r in errors\n        ),\n        \"error_sampler_worse\": sum(\n            r[\"sampler_only_iou\"] < r[\"selected_iou\"] for r in errors\n        ),\n        \"error_oracle_larger\": sum(\n            r[\"oracle_area\"] > r[\"selected_area\"] for r in errors\n        ),\n        \"error_largest_better\": sum(\n            r[\"largest_mask_iou\"] > r[\"selected_iou\"] for r in errors\n        ),\n        \"error_largest_worse\": sum(\n            r[\"largest_mask_iou\"] < r[\"selected_iou\"] for r in errors\n        ),\n        \"rows\": rows,\n    }\n    Path(args.output).write_text(json.dumps(result, indent=2), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    print(json.dumps({k: v for k, v in result.items() if k != \"rows\"}))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content -Raw pipeline/designs/exp_design_20260926-150100.md'","aggregated_output":"# Experiment Design - AdaRES_project\n\n2026-09-26 15:01 Asia/Shanghai\n\n## 1. Motivation\nGoal: \"AdaRES: improve a faithful standard-indicator 3D referring expression segmentation baseline by learning query confidence from metric-aligned evidence, targeting ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.515.\" Capacity 1/2, admission budget one. K1/K2 diagnose distinct potential shortcuts in B4 selection rather than propose tuning values.\n\n## 2. Current Best Results\n| ID | State | mIoU | Acc@0.25 | Acc@0.5 | spmIoU |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| B1 | complete | 0.5020 | 0.610 | 0.553 | 0.467 |\n| B4-E30 | champion | 0.5094 | 0.608 | 0.562 | 0.474 |\n| H5 | early stop | 0.5061 | unavailable | unavailable | unavailable |\n| G1 | training | 0.4983 interim best | unavailable | unavailable | unavailable |\n\n## 3. Analysis & Direction\nFixed 441-expression B4 subset: 240 material selection errors. K1 oracle is later than selected in 141/240 and has higher sampler score in 99/240; sampler-only subset mIoU 0.34587 versus indicator 0.49186. K2 oracle mask larger in 118/240, largest-mask mIoU 0.27271. Both hypothesized shortcuts lack directional support. Previous J1/J2 diagnoses and H1-H4 routes were already closed. G1 remains the only active test.\n\n## 4. Experiment Plan\nNo new experiment admitted. K1 and K2 fail diagnosis. Controls were native, but no candidate-specific backward, resource, independence, constraints or admission receipt are claimed as passed. Candidate budget is a maximum, not a quota. No rank/area fusion, threshold scan, seed repeat, ablation, H5 rename or B4 duplicate.\n\n## 5. GPU Allocation Plan\nServer-2 GPU0: G1 only. GPU1: vacant after read-only native diagnostics; targeted GPU check before screens showed 1 MiB and 0% utilization. Server-6 prohibited.\n\n## 6. Implementation Checklist\n- [x] Fixed 16-scene read-only paired diagnosis and sampler/area controls.\n- [x] Reject both mechanisms as stated and preserve hashed evidence.\n- [ ] No candidate model/config, receipt, commit/sync or queue push without all six gates.\n- [ ] Reassess G1 after terminal reconciliation or a genuinely independent new diagnosis.\n\n## 7. Risk Assessment\nThe subset is observational, not a population efficacy estimate. Sampler index correlates with learned relevance but is not proof of rank use. Mask area is an incomplete quality surrogate. G1 may change the bottleneck; its terminal metrics are pending. No model resource profile exists for K1/K2 because neither proceeds.\n\n## 8. Smell Check\nA rank penalty, area correction, mixing coefficient, or threshold would be tuning-only without new evidence and graph structure. None is admitted.\n\nStatus: NO ADMISSION. Stop after two distinct executable diagnoses were disconfirmed; this is not global exhaustion. Resume at G1 terminal outcome or new independent evidence with a concrete candidate and matched control.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
